{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Psalm 144:5</b> הט — an allusion to the decrees that come, destined, from the heavens. And the meaning of גע בהרים — in the fire that descends. Therefore ויעשנו — and the meaning is that the mountains, which stand firm, if You touch them they are immediately consumed, all the more so man who is nothingness."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 144, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:39.893580114Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}